IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wra-types`
IMPORT `wra-universal-credit`
IMPORT `wra-pip`
IMPORT `wra-cap`

-- Welfare Reform Act 2012 (UK) — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Welfare case` HAS
    `a universal credit claim`                          IS A MAYBE `Universal credit claim`
    `a PIP claim`                                       IS A MAYBE `PIP facts`
    `the benefit cap facts`                             IS A MAYBE `Cap facts`

DECLARE `Welfare position` HAS
    `entitled to universal credit`                      IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `universal credit award`                            IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `PIP daily living component`                        IS A MAYBE `Component rate`
    `PIP mobility component`                            IS A MAYBE `Component rate`
    `benefit cap reduction`                             IS A MAYBE NUMBER

@ref ss 3-5, 8, 77-83, 96
@export default The position under the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (UK): whether universal credit is payable and the award (ss 3-5, 8; the award is 0 where not entitled); the personal independence payment components and rates (ss 77-83); and the benefit cap reduction (s 96). Each is NOTHING where its facts are not given. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Welfare case`  @desc Any universal credit claim, any PIP claim, and the benefit cap facts
GIVETH A `Welfare position`
`the welfare position for` c MEANS
    `Welfare position` WITH
        `entitled to universal credit`                  IS
            CONSIDER c's `a universal credit claim`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST u  THEN JUST (`is entitled to universal credit` u)
        `universal credit award`                        IS
            CONSIDER c's `a universal credit claim`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST u  THEN JUST (IF `is entitled to universal credit` u THEN `the universal credit award for` u ELSE 0)
        `PIP daily living component`                    IS
            CONSIDER c's `a PIP claim`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST f  THEN JUST (`the daily living component for` f)
        `PIP mobility component`                        IS
            CONSIDER c's `a PIP claim`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST f  THEN JUST (`the mobility component for` f)
        `benefit cap reduction`                         IS
            CONSIDER c's `the benefit cap facts`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST f  THEN JUST (`the benefit cap reduction for` f)
